# The Northrop Grumman B-2A Spirit's checklists: this project's own, in its own words.
#
# **They are not taken from the aeroplane's flight manual.** No such
# manual was read to write them. What they follow is the ordinary
# practice for the type, in the order it is flown; the speeds and
# settings in them are this project's own figures, assets/figures/b2.xml,
# whose sources docs/ASSETS.md records, and the flight model itself
# wherever the model is what decides - a lever's gate, a flap's travel,
# an engine's idle.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# The flying wing has no tail, and the model gives it no flap lever and no
# speedbrake lever: its elevons do the work of elevator, aileron and flap
# together, and its split drag rudders answer the rudder pedals rather than a
# lever of their own. So nothing here names a flap or a speedbrake setting,
# and what a pilot would do with them is left as the pilot's to confirm. Its
# four F118s are unaugmented: there is no reheat to check either.

phase before-start
confirm Walk-round done, the bay doors shut and the aeroplane clear to start
confirm Both crew strapped in, harnesses tight and the ejection seat pins stowed
confirm Oxygen on and both masks checked
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.05 All four throttles closed
check gear/gear-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage lever down
confirm Batteries and ground power on, and the engine bays called clear

phase taxi
check propulsion/engine[0]/n1 >= 35.0 Port outer engine running
check propulsion/engine[3]/n1 >= 35.0 Starboard outer engine running
confirm All four engines' gauges reading alike as they settle at idle
confirm Brakes checked as the aeroplane first moves
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.40 Taxi at a walking pace on low power

phase take-off
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Elevon trim set for the take-off
confirm Controls free and correct, and the take-off briefed
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked for the roll
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.95 All four throttles fully forward
check velocities/vc-kts >= 140.0 Ease the nose up at 140 knots

phase climb
check gear/gear-cmd-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage lever up
check gear/gear-pos-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage locked up, which takes eight seconds
range velocities/vc-kts 250.0 330.0 Climb at 250 to 320 knots
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.85 Climb power set
confirm Temperatures and pressures in the green on all four engines

phase cruise
range velocities/mach 0.70 0.85 High subsonic, Mach 0.70 to 0.85
range position/h-sl-ft 35000.0 50000.0 Level between 35,000 and 50,000 feet
check gear/gear-pos-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage up
confirm Altimeter set, and the wing trimmed to hold its height
confirm Fuel balanced across the four tanks

phase descent
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.0 0.60 Throttles back for the descent
check velocities/vc-kts <= 340.0 Down at no more than 340 knots
confirm Altimeter set to the field's pressure
confirm Nothing but the drag rudders to slow this wing, so the descent is begun early
confirm Approach briefed and the landing weight known

phase approach
check gear/gear-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage lever down
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked
range velocities/vc-kts 140.0 170.0 Approach at 140 to 170 knots
confirm Landing lights on and the runway in sight
confirm Runway length checked against the landing weight

phase landing
range velocities/vc-kts 130.0 150.0 Over the threshold at 130 to 150 knots
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.25 Throttles closed in the flare
confirm Hold the nose wheel off, lower it gently, then brake straight

phase after-landing
check position/h-agl-ft <= 50.0 Down and rolling
check velocities/vc-kts <= 40.0 Clear of the runway and slowed to a taxi
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.35 Throttles back to a taxi power
confirm Landing lights off and the bay doors confirmed shut
